.TH "OSTRYA\-REV\-PARSE" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-rev\-parse \- Print the commit checksum that a revision names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya rev\-parse [OPTIONS] [REV]...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the commit checksum that a revision names.
.PP
The command prints one \%64\-character checksum on each line, one for each REV, in order. A revision that does not resolve is an error. \%\-\-single prints the one commit object of the repository and takes no REV.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIREV...\fR
The revisions to resolve. Required, unless \%\-\-single is given.
.IP
A revision is a full checksum, an abbreviated checksum of \%1 to \%63 lowercase hex characters, or a refspec. An abbreviated checksum must match exactly one commit. Each trailing \fB\%^\fR steps back one generation of ancestry. The command prints one commit checksum for each revision, in order.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-single\fR
Print the one commit of the repository.
.IP
An empty repository is an error, and so is a repository with more than one commit. The command refuses a REV argument with this switch.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
